# Build context exclusions.
#
# The one that matters: **/node_modules. The frontend stage installs from the
# lockfile with `npm ci`, and the `COPY frontend/ ./` after it would otherwise
# copy a local `frontend/node_modules` over that install, shipping whatever is
# on the build host instead of the pinned tree. `.gitignore` excluding
# node_modules does not keep it out of the build context.
**/node_modules

# Built frontend assets: the frontend stage produces these itself, and a stale
# local `dist` copied over a fresh build has the same failure mode as above.
frontend/dist

# Python build/venv/cache artefacts — never wanted in a build context.
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
*.egg-info

# Operator-local state. `var/` holds the code mirrors, checkouts and vector backups: large,
# machine-specific, and never needed at build time.
var/

# Secrets must not enter the build context even though no COPY references them.
.env
.env.*

# VCS and CI metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Screenshots: the image ships the docs for help.search and help.get, which read Markdown only.
docs/images/
